  "remainingSection4DeductiveGaps": [
    "Lemma 4.8 standalone secant-to-C1 criterion for an arbitrary topological hypersurface",
    "A mathlib manifold-with-boundary structure on each dual ball, beyond the proved local one-sided C1 graphs"
  ],
  "section4ScopeIssue": "The weak-distance description of union-defined dual inflation fails for arbitrary nonclosed sets when the infimum is not attained. The union/preimage identities and nonempty compact/closed corrections are proved; the compact-set dual theory is not refuted.",
  "section4ProofStrategy": "Theorem 4.10 uses the proved local-maximizer transport induction followed by nearest-point quadratic maxima and compactness of the projected transported initial normal bundle. No manuscript edit was made. Theorem 4.9 now uses an actual regular-closed-frontier projection proof and a quantitative zero-radius small/large-radius estimate. The dual normal correspondences use tangent-set normal comparison, without differentiating the distance function. No manuscript proof has been edited. Round three separately proves distance differentiability using compact-gap nearest-point convergence and a squared-distance sandwich, with a closed/proper localization extension. The inverse exponential display uses the genuine unit-bundle inverse. No manuscript proof has been edited.",
